      "writtenOn": "2023-11-14T00:09:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a good question.\n\nMy opinion is the constant `build_info` also contains the full string of `VERSION` from the generated `ec_version.h`. The full version can be checked in some alternative way, just not so straightforward in the RW_FWID. A dev build is probably fine.\n\nA follow-up task is to repurpose the `image_data.cros_fwid[32]` as an extension of `image_data.version[32]`. So the `version` console command will show a 63-character string.\n\nOr people have other ideas?",
      "parentUuid": "f48214bf_b3078d69",
      "revId": "b484aea0d44c5d61165f01bc58e9fefb5bfbdae6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
